1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,950
Lesson 13: the other functions for HF

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:15,589
YA-NEC course, lesson 13: the other functions for HF. Examples: the ARRL 520-40H, a 5-element Yagi for 20 m at 70 ft, from the ARRL Antenna Book.

3
00:00:15,639 --> 00:00:25,989
65 wires of telescoping aluminium tubing, with the Leeson correction for the steps. The cards on top: 21.5 - j16.6 ohm, 15.06 dBi, F/B 28 dB.

4
00:00:26,039 --> 00:00:34,723
SWR 2.64 on 50 ohm: the ARRL design needs its own match (hairpin or gamma). The model shows the bare driven element.

5
00:00:34,773 --> 00:00:41,790
Patterns tab: azimuth at the elevation of the maximum, and elevation in the main direction.

6
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:51,790
Maximum at 13.2 degrees over average ground, -3 dB beamwidth 55.1 degrees in azimuth and 14.2 in elevation, the ARRL logarithmic scale.

7
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:58,923
'Azimuth rotated by 90 degrees': 0 degrees at the top or on the right, as in EZNEC or MMANA.

8
00:00:58,973 --> 00:01:06,657
Same pattern, different habit.

9
00:01:06,707 --> 00:01:16,605
Linear scale in dB: the rear lobes look much bigger, because the ARRL scale compresses the low levels.

10
00:01:16,655 --> 00:01:20,673
Frequency tab: the sweep over the band.

11
00:01:20,723 --> 00:01:30,806
SWR, gain in the main direction, impedance, F/B and F/R, radiation efficiency: across 14.0-14.4 MHz the F/B peaks at 35 dB near 14.1 MHz.

12
00:01:30,856 --> 00:01:33,873
The 'More data' card.

13
00:01:33,923 --> 00:01:43,006
Efficiency 98.5 % (losses in the aluminium), 145 segments. The AGT test only applies in free space or over perfect ground.

14
00:01:43,056 --> 00:01:47,072
Smith chart.

15
00:01:47,122 --> 00:01:56,138
The impedance from 14.0 (green) to 14.4 MHz (orange) with the SWR 2 circle: everything a matching network has to correct.

16
00:01:56,188 --> 00:02:00,339
NEC tab: the NEC-2 cards of the model, editable.

17
00:02:00,389 --> 00:02:10,339
Here you can read and change every card - GW, GE, GN, EX, LD, FR - then 'Apply and recalculate'. Comments keep the source of the model.

18
00:02:10,389 --> 00:02:15,472
Noise/GT/Stack: the receive side, antenna temperature and G/T.

19
00:02:15,522 --> 00:02:24,872
Below 28 MHz the program warns: external noise dominates, so G/T is only for comparison. It becomes useful in VHF - lesson 18.

20
00:02:24,922 --> 00:02:30,873
Patterns, sweep, Smith, more data, NEC cards: the tools around the simulation. Next lesson: the DK7ZB 6-element Yagi with the designer's dimensions. 73 de IC8TEM
